{"name":"Golden Trident","hex":"#e8c954","fetched":"2026-10-12","looked":{"definitions":[{"term":"golden","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Adjective","definitions":["Made of, or relating to, gold.","Having a color or other richness suggestive of gold."]},{"part":"Noun","definitions":["(Can we verify this sense?) brassy drummer, brassy chub, etc. (Kyphosus vaigiensis), a fish found in southeast Asia.","Ellipsis of golden retriever."]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/golden"},{"term":"trident","whole":false,"parts":[{"part":"Noun","definitions":["A three-pronged spear somewhat resembling a pitchfork.","A curve of third order of the form:"]}],"link":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/trident"}],"entries":[{"title":"Trident","blocks":[{"text":"A trident is a three-pronged spear. It is used for spear fishing and historically as a polearm. As compared to an ordinary spear, the three tines increase the chance that a fish will be struck and decrease the chance that a fish will be able to dislodge itself if struck badly. On the other hand, they are not so many as to overly reduce the spear's concentration of force for piercing."}],"image":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/b/b1/Poseidon_sculpture_Copenhagen_2005_hand.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail_unscaled","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Trident","wikidata":"Q271628"},{"title":"Gold (color)","blocks":[{"text":"Gold, also called golden, is a color tone resembling the chemical element gold."}],"image":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5b/GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg/330px-GoldNuggetUSGOV.jpg?utm_source=en.wikipedia.org&utm_campaign=api&utm_content=thumbnail","link":"https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Gold_(color)","wikidata":"Q208045"}],"images":[{"srcset":"https://thumb.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/thumb/5/5a/%E6%AD%A6%E5%82%99%E5%BF%97_%E8%8C%85%E5%85%83%E5%84%80_%E6%98%8E%E6%9C%9D%E5%85%AD_48.jpg/500px-%E6%AD%A6%E5%82%99%E5%BF%97_%E8%8C%85%E5%85%83%E5